        "System.CommentCount": 0,
        "System.Title": "FastAPI-Based API Platform Implementation",
        "Microsoft.VSTS.Common.StateChangeDate": "2026-10-23T15:43:31.41Z",
        "Microsoft.VSTS.Common.Priority": 1,
        "Microsoft.VSTS.Scheduling.TargetDate": "2026-11-15T00:00:00Z",
        "Microsoft.VSTS.Scheduling.StartDate": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z",
        "System.Description": "<div><p dir=ltr><strong>Goal</strong><br>\nDesign and deliver an API layer based on FastAPI that enables integration of [system/module] with [external systems / frontend / other services] in a secure, scalable, and well-documented way. </p><p dir=ltr><strong>Scope</strong> </p><ul dir=ltr><li>Set up the FastAPI project (structure, dependencies, environment configuration) </li><li>Implement endpoints for key functionality </li><li>Validate request and response data (Pydantic) </li><li>Implement authentication and authorization </li><li>Add error handling and logging </li><li>Provide API documentation (OpenAPI/Swagger) </li><li>Write unit and integration tests </li><li>Containerize the service and configure the CI/CD pipeline </li><li>Deploy to DEV/TEST/PROD environments </li> </ul><p dir=ltr><strong>Out of scope</strong> </p><ul dir=ltr><li>[e.g. changes to existing business logic] </li><li>[e.g. migration of historical data] </li> </ul><p dir=ltr><strong>Acceptance criteria</strong> </p><ul dir=ltr><li>All defined endpoints are available and behave according to the specification </li><li>OpenAPI documentation is generated and up to date </li><li>Test coverage meets the agreed threshold (e.g. ≥ 80%) </li><li>The CI/CD pipeline builds, tests, and deploys the service automatically </li><li>Integration with [target system] is verified in the test environment </li><li>Monitoring and logging are operational in production </li> </ul><p dir=ltr><strong>Dependencies and risks</strong> </p><ul dir=ltr><li>Availability of the API contract/specification from team [X] </li><li>Access to environments and secrets </li><li>Performance under expected load </li> </ul><br> </div>",
        "System.Tags": "DoD required; UAT_first"
    },
